From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TurboVadim <yolkin.vadim@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 22:48:03 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Count spawning mobs without per-entity callbacks

Resolve synchronous counting chunks directly from fullChunks and share the
counting body with the generic ChunkGetter path. Keep separate captures for
generic queries, which may invoke their callbacks later.

Preserve entity order, persistence and spawn-reason filters, loaded-chunk
membership, biome charges, category counts and per-player attribution. Keep
async counting disabled by default.

The measured candidate also held a biome-lookup hint, dropped for having no
measured effect. It passed 13 focused tests and all seven behavior digest
checks. Six interleaved idle-survival runs per jar measured
9.616 -> 9.229 mspt, -4.03% +/- 6.89% at 95%, and 2313.704 -> 1936.051 KB/t,
-16.32% +/- 2.91%. Moving-player timing was +0.35% +/- 6.09%. These results
measure the combined candidate, not this patch in isolation.

